  "description": {
   "text": "Conjure Earth Elemental\n(Conjuration/Summoning)\n\nLevel: 7\nSphere: Elemental (Earth), Summoning\nRange: Visual range of the caster\nDuration: 1 turn/level\nCasting Time: 9\nArea of Effect: Special\nSaving Throw: None\n\nUpon casting a Conjure Earth Elemental spell, the caster opens a special gate to the Elemental Plane of Earth, and an earth elemental is summoned in the vicinity of the caster. The chance of summoning a 12-, 16-, or 24-Hit-Dice elemental scales with caster level from 64% / 35% / 1% at 11th level (61% / 37% / 2% at 12th, 52% / 42% / 6% at 15th) up to 37% / 51% / 12% at 20th level. All of the commands given to the elemental are done telepathically, so there is no time lost due to miscommunication, and it is not necessary to know the language of the summoned creature. Unlike Mages, priests do not have to engage in a battle of the minds to control their summoned elemental.",
   "old": 15181
